  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Show that the following equations are consistent: 2x + 3y + 4 = 0; x + 2y + 3 = 0; 3x + 4y + 5 = 0. (3 marks)', 'Solve the first two: 2x + 3y = −4 and x + 2y = −3. From the second, x = −3 − 2y; substituting, 2(−3 − 2y) + 3y = −4, so −6 − y = −4, y = −2 and x = 1. Check in the third: 3(1) + 4(−2) + 5 = 3 − 8 + 5 = 0 ✓. All three lines pass through (1, −2), so the equations are consistent. (Equivalently, the determinant |2 3 4; 1 2 3; 3 4 5| = 2(10 − 12) − 3(5 − 9) + 4(4 − 6) = −4 + 12 − 8 = 0.)', null, '[{"point": "Solve two equations: from 2x + 3y = −4 and x + 2y = −3: x = 1, y = −2", "marks": 1.5}, {"point": "Substitute in third: 3(1) + 4(−2) + 5 = 0 ✓ (or determinant of augmented coefficients = 0) → consistent, unique solution", "marks": 1.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
