  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Answer the following questions.

a) When a glass rod is rubbed with a silk cloth, charges appear on both. A similar phenomenon is observed with many other pairs of bodies. Explain how this observation is consistent with the law of conservation of charge. (1.5 marks)', 'a) Rubbing does not create charge; it transfers electrons from one body to the other. Electrons move from the glass rod to the silk, so the glass becomes positively charged and the silk acquires an equal negative charge. The total charge of the isolated system (glass + silk) remains zero before and after, as the law of conservation of charge requires.', null, '[{"point": "Rubbing transfers electrons from glass to silk; glass becomes positive and silk equally negative; total charge stays zero - charge is neither created nor destroyed, only transferred", "marks": 1.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
